 :change
 "`scan*` asked `(satisfies? IPatternSource db)` on every call -- once per
  distinct substituted pattern, ~1,800 times per IC02. `q` now decides once and
  binds it. Measured cost of the check: 11,305 ns against 210 ns for the index
  read it guarded."

 :paired-p50-ratio-kotobase-over-neo4j
 {:ic02 {:before 9.710 :after 3.073}
  :ic07 {:before 0.995 :after 0.838}
  :ic08 {:before 1.855 :after 1.955}
  :ic09 {:before 8.641 :after 7.382}
  :before-source "2026-08-13-planner-estimate-ab.edn, arm A"}

 :absolute-p50-ms
 {:kotobase {:ic02 6.259 :ic07 0.449 :ic08 0.769 :ic09 137.388}
  :neo4j-embedded {:ic02 2.203 :ic07 0.515 :ic08 0.449 :ic09 18.809}
  :note "Interleaved per sample in one JVM. Absolutes move with host load; the
         paired ratio is the column that survives."}

 :reading
 "IC02 falls from 9.7x to 3.1x. IC07 goes below 1.0 -- kotobase answers it faster
  than embedded Neo4j. IC09 improves less (8.6 -> 7.4) because its two-hop step
  substitutes to far fewer distinct patterns per binding than IC02's, so it was
  paying the check proportionally less. IC08 is unchanged within noise.

  The saving scales with the number of DISTINCT substituted patterns a query
  scans, which is exactly what the diagnosis predicted and why a single-clause
  query saw nothing."

 :what-this-is-not
 ["Not an LDBC score. Four Interactive Complex reads on a deterministic subset of
   SF1, not the certified driver over the full workload with an auditor."
  "Not a claim of parity overall. IC02 is still 3.1x and IC09 still 7.4x."
  "Answers asserted equal to Neo4j's on all four queries, as the harness requires."]}
